    "tagid": "MQBXJF97E",
    "message": "[SIZE=4][COLOR=#ff0000]\u26a0 Note:\n* Performance may degrade when many traffic vehicles are spawned simultaneously. If you experience frame rate drops, try reducing the number of spawned vehicles.[\/COLOR][\/SIZE]\n[B][SIZE=5]\nOverview:[\/SIZE][\/B]\nI modified original [I]\"Kick Plate\"[\/I] prop into [I]\"Gimmick Pad\"[\/I].\n\nGimmick Pad is a mod that adds a special pad object to BeamNG.drive. Any vehicle that drives over the pad triggers a gimmick \u2014 a wide variety of effects ranging from speed boosts and flips to explosions and teleportation.\n\nThis mod is the official successor to the original Dash Plate mod, evolving far beyond its speed-only roots with over 30 different configurations.\n[ATTACH]1297706[\/ATTACH]\n\n[B]Introduction video by other creator:[\/B]\n[MEDIA=youtube]wUl-b0103Ug[\/MEDIA]\n\n[HR][\/HR]\n[B][SIZE=5]How to Use:[\/SIZE][\/B]\n[MEDIA=youtube]bvgKlYMPDjY[\/MEDIA]\nJust spawn it and it will work.\n[LIST=1]\n[*]Open the vehicle selector\n[*]Select a Gimmick Pad (Props section)\n[*]Select a preset configuration that matches the gimmick you want.\n[\/LIST]\nTo customize the gimmick and appearance, open Vehicle Configuration:\n[LIST]\n[*]Parts \u2014 Skin: Changes the marking displayed on the pad surface.\n\n[*]Parts \u2014 Gimmick: Switches the active gimmick effect.\n\n[*]Tuning: Adjusts parameters such as power, direction, and speed (varies by gimmick).\n\n[*]Color \u2014 Paint 1: Changes the pad body color.\n[\/LIST]\n[SPOILER=\"Advanced:\"]\n[B]Parameter override[\/B]\nTo set parameters beyond the tuning slider limits, use the vehicle Lua console:\n[CODE]controller.getController('executeFunction').setParam('dashplateSpeedKMH', 9999)[\/CODE]\n\n[B]Scan mode[\/B]\nThis mod supports two scan modes that control which side \u2014 the pad or the vehicle \u2014 is responsible for detecting proximity. The default [B]dashplate[\/B] mode works well for most cases. Switching to [B]vehicle[\/B] mode may improve performance when a large number of pads are placed in the world.\n\nSwitch modes from the [B]GE Lua console[\/B]:\n[CODE]extensions.mathkuro_dashplate.setScanMode('vehicle')   -- vehicle-side scanning\nextensions.mathkuro_dashplate.setScanMode('dashplate')  -- pad-side scanning (default)[\/CODE]\n\nThe mode resets to [B]dashplate[\/B] whenever the extension is reloaded.\n[\/SPOILER]\n\n[HR][\/HR]\n\n[H1]UI App (for Random)[\/H1]\nThis mod includes a HUD app that displays the gimmick icon triggered by a [B]Random[\/B] pad. When your vehicle drives over a Random pad, the icon of the selected effect appears on screen for 3 seconds.\n\n[B]How to enable:[\/B]\n[LIST=1]\n[*]Open the [B]Apps[\/B] menu (default: Home key).\n[*]Find [B]Gimmick Pad[\/B] in the app list and drag it onto the HUD.\n[\/LIST]\n\nThe app only reacts to effects triggered on your own vehicle. It has no effect when using non-Random configurations.\n\n[HR][\/HR]\n\n[H1]Configurations[\/H1]\n\n[SPOILER=\"Configurations\"]\n[B]\u2014 Speed & Movement \u2014[\/B]\n[LIST]\n[*][B]Boost (100km\/h, 62mph)[\/B] \u2014 Accelerates the vehicle to 100 km\/h.\n[*][B]Boost (200km\/h, 125mph)[\/B] \u2014 Accelerates the vehicle to 200 km\/h.\n[*][B]Boost (300km\/h, 186mph)[\/B] \u2014 Accelerates the vehicle to 300 km\/h.\n[*][B]Boost (500km\/h, 310mph)[\/B] \u2014 Accelerates the vehicle to 500 km\/h.\n[*][B]Boost (999km\/h, 620mph)[\/B] \u2014 Accelerates the vehicle to 999 km\/h.\n[*][B]Jump[\/B] \u2014 Launches the vehicle into the air.\n[*][B]One Way[\/B] \u2014 Pushes the vehicle in the direction the pad faces.\n[*][B]Reverse[\/B] \u2014 Sends the vehicle in the opposite direction.\n[*][B]Stop[\/B] \u2014 Instantly stops the vehicle.\n[*][B]Turn Left[\/B] \u2014 Steers the vehicle to the left.\n[*][B]Turn Right[\/B] \u2014 Steers the vehicle to the right.\n[*][B]Sling Shot[\/B] \u2014 Pulls the vehicle back, then launches it forward at high speed.\n[*][B]Speed x2[\/B] \u2014 Multiplies the vehicle's current speed by a configurable factor (default: \u00d72).\n[\/LIST]\n\n[B]\u2014 Damage & Chaos \u2014[\/B]\n[LIST]\n[*][B]Break Hinges[\/B] \u2014 Breaks all hinges on the vehicle.\n[*][B]Break Random Parts[\/B] \u2014 Randomly breaks structural parts of the vehicle.\n[*][B]Deflate Tires[\/B] \u2014 Deflates all tires.\n[*][B]Engine Stall[\/B] \u2014 Stalls the vehicle's engine.\n[*][B]Explode[\/B] \u2014 Triggers an explosion on the vehicle.\n[*][B]Ignite[\/B] \u2014 Sets the vehicle on fire.\n[\/LIST]\n\n[B]\u2014 Physics Effects \u2014[\/B]\n[LIST]\n[*][B]Flip(Front)[\/B] \u2014 Applies a forward or backward flipping torque.\n[*][B]Flip(Side)[\/B] \u2014 Applies a sideways flipping torque.\n[*][B]Spin Out[\/B] \u2014 Applies a horizontal spinning force.\n[*][B]Tornado[\/B] \u2014 Combines spin with an upward launch.\n[*][B]Fireworks[\/B] \u2014 Launches the vehicle straight up, then explodes it after a short delay.\n[\/LIST]\n\n[B]\u2014 Utility \u2014[\/B]\n[LIST]\n[*][B]Repair[\/B] \u2014 Repairs the vehicle at a configurable interval.\n[*][B]Extinguish[\/B] \u2014 Extinguishes fire on the vehicle.\n[*][B]Open[\/B] \u2014 Opens all latches (doors, hood, trunk).\n[*][B]Toggle Lights[\/B] \u2014 Turns on headlights, fog lights, hazard lights, and beacon.\n[*][B]Horn[\/B] \u2014 Continuously sounds the vehicle's horn.\n[*][B]Random Paint[\/B] \u2014 Applies a random paint color to the vehicle.\n[*][B]Teleport[\/B] \u2014 Teleports the vehicle. Gate number 0 sends it to a random spawn point; numbers 1\u2013100 teleport it to another pad with the matching gate number (falls back to random if none exists).\n[\/LIST]\n\n[B]\u2014 Special \u2014[\/B]\n[LIST]\n[*][B]Random[\/B] \u2014 Applies one randomly selected effect. The chance weighting for each effect is tunable. The included HUD app displays which effect was selected (see [B]UI App[\/B] section above).\n[*][B](Debug) All Functions[\/B] \u2014 Triggers all effects simultaneously. Intended for testing purposes.\n[\/LIST]\n\n[B]\u2014 Base Types (for World Building) \u2014[\/B]\n[LIST]\n[*][B]Flat[\/B] \u2014 A simple flat plate. Suitable for accelerating any type of object. [I](Deprecated \u2014 kept for backward compatibility)[\/I]\n[*][B](Invisible) Flat[\/B] \u2014 A flat plate with no visible mesh.\n[*][B]Slope[\/B] \u2014 A plate with a slight slope, usable as a speed bump replacement. [I](Deprecated \u2014 kept for backward compatibility)[\/I]\n[*][B](Invisible) Slope[\/B] \u2014 A slope plate with no visible mesh. [I](Deprecated \u2014 kept for backward compatibility)[\/I]\n[\/LIST]\n[\/SPOILER]\n\n[HR][\/HR]\nSupport me and get access to early versions of the mods here\n[URL]https:\/\/ko-fi.com\/mathkuro[\/URL]",
